record(s,t,r,d,inv,'The page introduces the integer ring as an algebra and an associated ring scheme, its unit group scheme, E and E^0, then a proposed description involving the abelianized Galois group and Pic(A). The author writes “vérifier ce pt.” beside the quotient and connected-component instruction. He then writes “semble être” for G^0=A*/R, defining R by closure of the unit sections and discussing its generic fibre. These are recorded as his formulations, without a proof check of the class-field or motivic claims. The ink reads “absolues”, not the alternative positives supplied by H. The small bound between α and r_1 is newly marked as strict/non-strict uncertainty; no mathematical expectation has supplied an extra equality stroke. In the second quotient the argument is literally Z×R*, with no hat on Z; that expression is retained together with the cancelled earlier argument. Archive number 158.',doubts=[['159','bound on index exponent',r'α\unsure{<|\leq}r_1','Nearly upright compressed stroke; separate equality rule not discernible.','low'],['159','cancelled argument of A*',r'\unsure{\mathbf A_{\mathbf Q}}','Dense diagonal hatching covers the main symbol; Q is lower right.','low'],['159','cancelled word after slash',r'\unsure{composante}','Initial c and descending p survive, much of ending is covered.','medium']],notation=[['Unit group schemes',r'\uuline{A}^*, \uuline{K}^*','159','Double underline consistently denotes the scheme letters.'],['Closure of unit sections',r'\mathcal R','159','Two large looped R occurrences.']],hand=['The initial ab in absolues has a low a and a tall b; H’s positives has no matching initial p descender.','Calligraphic R has several left loops and a curved right leg; H read N, but the bowl and leg recur in both occurrences.','Retracing in sections does not cross the word with an independent cancellation stroke.'],abbreviations=[['nbs.','nombres'],['alg.','algèbre'],['gén.','générique'],['pt.','point']],extra='Certainty-only: On and schéma are resolved. Cancelled composante remains doubtful after crop scan 159 (807,1112,997,1179). The paper-clip outline at the upper left is a physical mark, not a manuscript drawing.')
